00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:52.769
What was His Origin Story You Ask?

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:56.780
Ronnie Raymond was a High School student who
was caught in a nuclear explosion with Nobel

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.859
Prize winning Physics Professor Martin Stein.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:06.960
As a result of the explosion they fused to
form Firestorm "The Nuclear Man".

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:15.030
Because professor Stein was unconscious during
the blast, whenever they formed Firestorm,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.390
he manifested as a ghostly head talking to
Ronnie.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:30.270
Ronnie was the one operating the controls
so to speak.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:38.220
This all started back in the late 1970s, then
this big thing happened where DC cancelled

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.130
most of it's ongoing series in what was later
called the DC Implosion.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.790
After that Firestorm was written into the
Justice League Comics and then later he got

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.200
his own short stories at the end of the Flash
Comics.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.780
Sometimes they'll do that with really popular
comics, add short stories for lesser characters

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:55.780
at the end.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.220
Like bonus stories.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.130
So there's a long history of Firestorm being
paired up with the Flash.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:05.760
So it's kind of historic letting the character
debut on The Flash instead of Arrow, even

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.480
though Arrow is the bigger show right now.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.250
The Firestorm character mostly was based out
of Ivy City and New York.

